WEBVTT

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:34.430
Today's Rock Lee is starting!

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:37.510
But this episode has a bit 
of a different flavor.

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:41.590
Yes, today's show draws 
from that new movie...

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:45.550
<i>This is bad, I totally forgot 
to buy this week's Jump!</i>

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:47.500
<i>I hope they still have some.</i>

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:54.170
<b>Shonen Jump</b>

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:57.130
<i>Yes! There's one left!</i>

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:01.250
Tenten?

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:02.910
Lee... You, too?

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:07.630
Good thing it was you I ran into.

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:10.270
Anyone else and it would've 
been a serious tug-of-war.

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:14.180
Yeah, now we'll both be able to read it.

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:15.320
Ready to―

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:17.970
What was that for?

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.450
My question exactly.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:22.250
Ladies first. Let me read it.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:25.660
Excuse me, aren't you the one who 
always says gender doesn't matter?!

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.540
You're going to read it on the toilet.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:30.290
You're going to read it in the bath.

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:32.440
Better than stinking it up!

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:34.710
I'm not reading a soggy magazine!

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:39.260
Let go! This issue has 
 info on the movie!

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:41.340
I know! That's exactly why...

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:44.320
I want the latest details right away!

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:14.080
What just happened?

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:16.090
It felt like the world turned 
inside-out for a second...

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:18.280
Don't panic.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:20.170
This has happened before.

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:29.020
Let's keep calm and find some water.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:31.440
No, no, no, you just had heatstroke.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:34.310
What are you two doing here?

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:36.230
Oh, good timing, Shino.

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:37.780
Something weird just happened―

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:40.610
But not as weird as your outfit!

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:41.720
What's that supposed to mean?

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:43.930
I'm just being flashy like usual!

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:47.040
I may be a ninja, but I don't 
blend in the background.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:48.540
That's the kind of man I am.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:49.840
I can't take my eyes off you,

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:51.910
and as the main character I'm 
jealous of your flashiness!

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:56.420
Lee and Naruto alone are all 
the flashy ninjas we need...

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:59.380
Did Shino get a concussion or something?

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:01.010
D-Don't stare...

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:01.920
Something wrong?

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.050
You're not usually so shy, Kiba.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:07.430
I'll answer for you.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.820
And it's not because I'm being nice,

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:13.390
but I can't depend on anyone else 
here, so I've got no choice!

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:15.220
Hinata's snapping at people?!

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:16.490
That's impossible!

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:17.990
What's wrong with everyone?!

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:19.820
There a problem?

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:23.040
Oh thank God, Shikamaru―

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:33.660
I... think a punchline would 
actually be inappropriate, right?

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:38.840
Whew, I cleaned up again today!

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.410
Yay, time to make the 
village a better place!

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:44.090
We're off to fight evil, don'tcha know!

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:48.550
What next? The world's
gone topsy-turvy!

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:49.790
I know just what to do.

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:52.310
At times like this, 
there's only one way out!

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:54.930
So, good night.

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:58.930
We're not in a dream!

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:01.030
Indeed.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:02.850
Be serious! This is not a normal crisis!

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:07.800
If we don't figure out what happened,
we could be stuck here forever!

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.470
Then let's move out.

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:10.810
Where to?

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.200
To find Neji.

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:15.930
We'll need help if we're going 
to figure out what happened.

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:16.710
But...

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:19.150
It'll be okay.

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:21.150
No matter how much the world's changed,

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:22.860
our friendship is unshakable.

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:26.680
<b>Hyuga</b>

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:26.130
No, no way.

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:27.340
Huh?!

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:29.890
The Dark Emperor appears!!

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:29.890
Tenten    |       Neji      | Rock Lee

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:30.370
Me and my friends from a previous life...

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:33.460
...are battling to save the 
world from the Dark Emperor.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:36.730
No matter what happens,
I can't abandon this fight.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.730
<b>Stay Out</b>

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:39.110
O-Our friendship...

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:41.320
I can't believe Neji's an
angsty teen gamer...

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:44.740
We're stuck. We'll have to 
look for clues on our own.

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:47.570
Neji, I'm leaving your dinner out here.

00:05:55.550 --> 00:05:58.440
I may have just the 
clue we're looking for.

00:05:58.440 --> 00:05:59.910
What is it?

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:01.040
Ah ha.

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:03.590
It's the exact same ramen.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:08.070
And the weird situation 
we've found ourselves in...

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:10.830
It's all just like the promotional 
material for the movie!

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:12.100
So you're saying...

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:15.680
I don't know how or why, 
but in that instant,

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.040
our wish to know what 
the movie would be like...

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:21.440
...was granted by this issue of Jump.

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:25.080
Maybe we've been transported 
into the world of the movie!

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:28.330
You really think it's possible?

00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:31.740
Let's do it, Tenten!

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:33.200
Right on!

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:36.790
Send us back!

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:40.720
Nothing.

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:42.520
Everything was exactly the same...

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:45.340
No, it's lacking something.

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:45.800
Huh?

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:48.060
The first time, we both longed to see...

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:50.720
...the sneak peek from the 
bottom of our hearts.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.510
Our souls burned with passion,

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:55.320
and we both refused to let
the other have the first look.

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:56.870
Like this!

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:04.710
Cut it out, you'll rip it!

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:08.900
I'm sorry...

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:12.410
You might be on to something, though.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:15.640
We need those strong emotions, 
we can't just follow a script...

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:16.620
Script...

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:18.950
That's brilliant!

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:21.920
What are you wearing?

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:26.630
Prepare for my "script rewrite" plan!

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:30.200
If we don't have the passion,

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.630
we'll just physically 
alter the situation!

00:07:32.630 --> 00:07:35.800
That's way too literal. It'll never work!

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:39.340
I'll make it work.

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:41.100
I'm not staying in this world!

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:45.810
The Neji I know is arrogant 
and wears boxers...

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:48.030
But he's a man who values friendship!

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:50.420
I'm bringing that Neji back!

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:02.620
Did... it work?

00:08:03.470 --> 00:08:05.830
Come out, Neji!

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:13.000
The explosion of youth!

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:16.300
That's not right! 
Neji's like Guy Sensei now!

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:20.250
One, two, one, two...

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:19.780
Lee, what did you do?!

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:23.030
Well, I was thinking 
really hard about Neji,

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:25.540
but I guess I missed 
the mark a little bit.

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:28.230
Anyways, it looks like 
this method is effective.

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:30.730
Next...

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:39.580
<i>Hinata, a quiet hard worker 
who never neglected training.</i>

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:42.500
<i>And Kiba and Shino, her loyal friends...</i>

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:48.430
<i>Come back!</i>

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:59.240
The explosion of youth!

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:00.430
Not more!

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:04.210
Why do all your mistakes 
turn them into Guy Sensei?!

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:05.940
It looks like Guy Sensei maintains...

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:08.900
...an inordinately large presence 
in my subconscious...

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:12.650
Guy Sensei is always with me.

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:14.580
The stronger the emotion,

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:16.590
the more entrenched he becomes.

00:09:18.170 --> 00:09:22.040
Then you should include Guy Sensei
and think of everyone.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:25.960
Wish to return to our old friends!

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:34.810
<i>I don't want this to go on any longer.</i>

00:09:35.480 --> 00:09:36.220
<i>I...</i>

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:39.180
<i>I want to go back to everyone!</i>

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:02.760
That was just like the first time...

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:06.080
Guys?

00:10:07.490 --> 00:10:09.590
You're back to normal!

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:16.670
Oh no! Everyone turned into Guy Sensei!

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:20.800
Even the normal villagers?!

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:23.760
Lee, this is ridiculous!

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:26.160
What?! Guy Sensei?!

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:28.470
What are you talking about? It's me.

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:30.340
You wear the exact same outfits!

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:33.720
Jeez, now your face looks like his, too...

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:35.030
Don't tell me...

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:37.110
No, I'm Guy Sensei, too!

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:41.700
Make it stop. Standards and practices 
is gonna yank us off the air!

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:44.100
The explosion of youth!

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:45.620
Youth!

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:46.830
Get away from me!

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:48.690
Why is this happening?

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:52.780
I just wanted to know about the movie!

00:10:53.390 --> 00:10:56.530
That's because the movie is...

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:05.640
"Naruto: Road to Guy!"

00:11:06.210 --> 00:11:07.550
It is not!

00:11:07.550 --> 00:11:10.750
That's not the movie's title!

00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:22.470
<b>Super Groovy Ramen</b>

00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:24.740
Now, about the new Naruto movie...

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:24.720
<b>Super Groovy Sales</b>

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:27.000
Everyone's heard all about it, right?

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:26.720
<b>Super Groovy Gyoza</b>

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:28.680
<b>Movie</b>

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:28.830
Movie, not groovy!

00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:33.010
Rock Lee and his pals are excited, too!

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:36.280
Neji, did you get the tickets?

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:37.250
Of course!

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:40.260
The entire Hyuga clan plans to attend.

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:44.950
Our special advance-sale 
tickets are in hand!

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:47.010
Neji, Lee, we've got a problem!

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:48.680
What's got you so worked up?

00:11:49.010 --> 00:11:51.270
A while ago, Lady Tsunade...

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:53.350
What?

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:57.020
You say the movie's still 
missing a critical piece?

00:11:57.490 --> 00:12:00.110
Yeah, something big, too.

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:03.330
That doesn't sound good.

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:05.070
Something's lacking.

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:09.750
Lacking... with the film?

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:19.800
<b>The Amazing True Story of the 
Leaf Village Film Festival!</b>

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:24.300
What could be missing?

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:27.180
So that's the problem...

00:12:27.530 --> 00:12:29.560
I've got it.

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:40.750
<i>Man, I've got no luck at all.</i>

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:43.780
<i>Here it is, Christmas Eve...</i>

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:47.770
<i>But I've gotta save my family.</i>

00:12:59.140 --> 00:13:00.650
What the heck is this?

00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:03.440
We just started this pointless 
skit for no reason!

00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:04.800
Don't you see, Tenten?

00:13:05.210 --> 00:13:08.760
The movie's missing a big 
Hollywood action sequence,

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:13.180
and a tough American hero 
who overcomes all odds!

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:14.720
No way, we don't need that mess!

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:16.060
An American hero?

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:18.940
Naruto's supposed to be the hero.

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:21.130
If you jump in like that 
you'll obliterate him!

00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:24.470
It's fine, the movie's a compilation 
of several arcs anyway!

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:26.890
Oh, yeah, what if the
enemy he's fighting...

00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:29.930
...eventually becomes his
most powerful ally?

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:34.410
What crazy direction are you 
trying to take the movie in?!

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.370
She's right, Lee.

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:39.310
You've got it all wrong.

00:13:39.310 --> 00:13:42.500
For starters, we haven't had one movie 
that's lacked in big action sequences!

00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:45.260
Then do you know what's missing, Neji?

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:45.970
Of course!

00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:49.680
What's lacking... is...

00:13:51.130 --> 00:13:53.310
O Nejio, Nejio...

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:56.140
Wherefore art thou, Nejio?

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:57.920
Hinaette...

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:00.060
My life were better ended, 
than death prorogued...

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:02.360
...wanting of thy love!

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:06.530
But the two young lovers belonged 
to houses embroiled in a feud...

00:14:07.170 --> 00:14:10.000
Their love doomed to fail.

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:11.980
And so the two of them...

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:16.500
O Nejio!

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:23.590
Hold the phone, why do we need this?

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:26.400
A fair maiden and her lover,

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:28.550
a fleeting romance, two soul 
mates fading into the night!

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:32.760
What's missing is melodrama!

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:36.770
This is a summer movie, no one 
wants to see a tearjerker now!

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:39.300
Precisely why we must have the 
courage to break the mold!

00:14:39.300 --> 00:14:41.540
The movie will go down in film history...

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:43.950
as a powerful drama that wrung
tears from the eyes of the audience,

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:45.010
a timeless piece that will 
forever remain a shining ex―

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:47.720
Go shine out in the stratosphere!

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:52.300
I've been listening to you guys, 
and you're all clueless.

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:54.490
You're saying you all have a better idea?

00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:55.990
Sure do!

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:57.230
Right, Hinata?

00:14:57.230 --> 00:14:58.410
W-Well...

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:02.170
Maybe a more innocent 
love is what's missing.

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:04.980
<b>"The most powerful film of this era." 
- Puko Film Critics ―</b>

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:07.590
<b>"The whole audience was bawling!" 
- Leaf Times ―</b>

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:12.120
It begins with a young love...

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:19.370
A girl with no courage,

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:21.630
who could only watch him from afar.

00:15:24.740 --> 00:15:26.900
But she had to change,

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:29.600
so he would finally notice her.

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:36.690
Welcome home.

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:43.540
<b>Ointment</b>

00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:48.300
Hinata

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:52.760
Please use that ointment, if you like.

00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:56.970
I've watched you since the 
day we met. I still am...

00:16:03.330 --> 00:16:05.380
<b>I only have <i>EYES</i> for you...</b>

00:16:11.670 --> 00:16:15.510
That's not innocent love!
That's a stalker horror flick!

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:16.910
Stalker?

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:20.750
That does it! I'll settle 
this once and for all!

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:22.290
This could be okay.

00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:24.670
We live in a world where...

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:27.740
...ninjas face one brutal 
mission after another.

00:16:27.740 --> 00:16:29.170
What we need is...

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:30.510
<b>Moe</b>

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:30.510
...moe!

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:37.930
Come on, Akamaru!

00:16:47.510 --> 00:16:48.610
Oh, you!

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:08.820
Wait, only the dog does the moe?

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:11.560
Well, duh. What's cuter than that?

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:13.670
Think of the audience, not just yourself!

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:15.300
People.

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:17.670
Your preoccupation with the superficial...

00:17:17.670 --> 00:17:19.640
...has caused you to
overlook something vital.

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:22.980
What's truly lacking here is...

00:17:23.440 --> 00:17:25.880
Man's true thoughts... Yes...

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:28.400
The voice of our hearts made clear.

00:17:29.420 --> 00:17:31.730
<i>Wow, that's Shino for you. He's deep!</i>

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:35.160
The weather was awful the 
day we filmed this scene.

00:17:35.550 --> 00:17:37.250
I can't tell you how many takes we did.

00:17:37.730 --> 00:17:40.300
Oh, yeah, we took lunch while we 
were waiting for it to clear up,

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:41.700
but mine was pretty light on the veggies.

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:45.010
Honestly, I wish I'd ordered a salad instead―

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:46.950
The "voice of your heart" is audio commentary?

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:48.490
Where's the problem?

00:17:48.490 --> 00:17:50.050
The whole thing's the problem!

00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:52.480
You can't have audio commentary 
over the theater shows!

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:53.280
Oh, Tenten.

00:17:53.280 --> 00:17:53.920
Huh?

00:17:54.320 --> 00:17:56.990
Yeah, I wanted to get 
this scene just right,

00:17:56.990 --> 00:17:58.890
so we shot a ton of takes, I―

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:00.850
Don't drag me into this!

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:04.430
What could possibly be missing?

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:05.520
You fools.

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:08.230
How can you not see it?

00:18:08.570 --> 00:18:10.820
Orochimaru! What're you doing here?!

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:12.030
Just dropping in.

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:15.440
We saw you idiots flailing 
about and couldn't resist.

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:17.450
Wait, then you know what 
the movie's missing?

00:18:17.680 --> 00:18:18.540
Silly child.

00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:21.450
You're completely forgetting.

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:24.290
There is one element essential to a film.

00:18:24.740 --> 00:18:26.720
One that must never be overlooked...

00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:29.380
The most important part of all!

00:18:30.430 --> 00:18:32.290
<b>Orochimaru</b>

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:34.790
And, action!

00:18:35.170 --> 00:18:37.210
I turn forty this year.

00:18:37.210 --> 00:18:40.610
I've spent my whole career as an 
actor playing no-name bit parts.

00:18:40.610 --> 00:18:43.220
I always considered myself to 
be dedicated to my craft...

00:18:43.220 --> 00:18:47.390
But one day I realized everyone 
around me was half my age.

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:50.980
I saw them striving for starring roles, 
while I just spun my wheels.

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:55.210
F-Fired?

00:18:55.210 --> 00:18:57.990
The thing is...
You're hard to work with.

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:00.840
Orosuke's takes things way too seriously.

00:19:02.930 --> 00:19:06.410
Orosuke's a nice man, but he's too pushy.

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:09.330
Fantasy!

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:09.330
The camera's over here!

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:14.090
<b>Sake             Beer</b>

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:14.090
<b>Pierrot</b>

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:11.380
We're closing, pal. Go home.

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:12.370
What'd you say to me?

00:19:12.370 --> 00:19:13.430
Enough!

00:19:14.690 --> 00:19:18.500
But even I found someone who loved me.

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:22.320
The sheltered daughter of a bigwig 
film distribution company president...

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:26.060
running off with a two-bit nobody like me.

00:19:26.730 --> 00:19:30.510
He objected, of course, so we ran off,

00:19:30.510 --> 00:19:33.410
but before we even had a chance 
to make one real memory...

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:35.020
I've gone back home.
-Kabuko

00:19:33.410 --> 00:19:36.160
I guess even common courtesy 
runs out eventually.

00:19:37.540 --> 00:19:39.490
Guess it's time to face the music.

00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:45.690
Dear! Dear!

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:47.790
You...

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:49.500
Why?

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:55.960
<b>Audition</b>

00:19:49.930 --> 00:19:51.990
What do you think of this role?

00:19:53.590 --> 00:19:55.490
You asked your father, didn't you?

00:19:56.680 --> 00:19:57.780
I had to.

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:01.380
At first he threatened to disown me,

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:05.020
but getting on my knees and 
begging was a small price to pay.

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:07.890
But why?

00:20:08.920 --> 00:20:10.140
I've seen it...

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:15.220
How brightly you shine when 
you're in front of the camera.

00:20:15.720 --> 00:20:19.010
And I want to see you shine 
from as close as possible.

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:19.900
That's all.

00:20:22.470 --> 00:20:28.120
<b>Audition</b>

00:20:28.440 --> 00:20:31.290
This should be good.
 Let's see what you're made of.

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:33.290
I'll do it.

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:35.350
No matter what it takes.

00:20:35.350 --> 00:20:36.650
Standby.

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:41.640
Watch! I'll shine like 
the sun for you, my love!

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:45.780
Too long!

00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:48.140
Wait, is this an anti-piracy commercial?!

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:51.310
Well? Without one of these 
you'd be in big trouble.

00:20:51.610 --> 00:20:54.670
Maybe so, but what does that 
have to do with the story?

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:56.010
Well done, Lord Orochimaru!

00:20:56.010 --> 00:20:57.840
Truly, you bring a whole new perspective!

00:20:57.840 --> 00:20:59.940
I'd say your perspective's truly skewed.

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:01.440
Give me a break!

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:03.640
What's this got to do 
with stopping piracy?

00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:06.870
You'll see. I'll explain 
everything shortly―

00:21:11.510 --> 00:21:13.110
We need an American hero!

00:21:13.110 --> 00:21:14.040
Melodrama!

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:14.730
Love...

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:16.100
Love!

00:21:17.760 --> 00:21:18.790
Dear me.

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:22.010
Well, what exactly was 
missing, Lady Tsunade?

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:24.340
It just got here, actually.

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:35.640
Everyone, make sure you go 
see the new Naruto movie!

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:37.820
Ah, it was the movie poster!

00:21:37.820 --> 00:21:40.830
See you at the theater, viewers!

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:44.370
Then that was all pointless?!

00:23:22.350 --> 00:23:25.690
Next time is "Boom!
The Shinobi Fireworks Show!"

00:23:23.130 --> 00:23:29.130
<b>Boom! The Shinobi Fireworks Show!
Bang! Tenten's Acting Weird!</b>

00:23:25.690 --> 00:23:29.130
and "Bang! Tenten's Acting Weird!"

00:23:29.130 --> 00:23:31.320
A fireworks show, I can't wait!

00:23:31.320 --> 00:23:33.000
With everyone off seeing the show,

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:34.840
I can get in a good nap.

00:23:34.840 --> 00:23:38.220
I hear the ramen's got 
a really unique flavor.

00:23:38.220 --> 00:23:42.160
Sakura's going to look so pretty with 
her face lit up by the sparklers!

00:23:42.160 --> 00:23:44.510
Isn't anyone going to look 
at the actual fireworks?!
